:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Docs",
    title: "Assets",
    summary: "Plugins emit stable asset metadata for stylesheets, SVGs, raster images, generated variants, and downloaded font files."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Asset Identity" }
    :markdown
      Klenod assets have two stable identifiers:

      - `logical_name`: the source-root-relative file path without import query parameters, such as `images/hero.png`.
      - `output_path`: the public content-hashed browser path, such as `/assets/hero.640w.abcd1234.png`.

      Query parameters configure an import without changing the logical name, so overlapping generated variants can be reused.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Lookup APIs" }
    :markdown
      The build graph and runtime bundle expose the same lookup shape.

      ```ruby
      context.asset("/assets/home.abc123.css")
      context.assets_for("styles/home.css")
      context.assets_for_module("pages/server.rb", type: :css)

      bundle.asset("/assets/home.abc123.css")
      bundle.assets_for_module("pages/server.rb", type: :css)
      ```

      `assets_for_module` is recursive by default. `asset_references_for_module` also includes a graph traversal index, which is useful for route-scoped CSS ordering.

  %DocsSection{ title: "CSS, SVG, And Images" }
    :markdown
      CSS imports from Ruby or Haml return class-name maps. CSS imports from CSS become stylesheet dependencies, and CSS `url(...)` references become asset dependencies.

      SVG imports emit the SVG file as a browser asset and export metadata with `src`, `width`, and `height`.

      Raster image imports support `.avif`, `.gif`, `.jpeg`, `.jpg`, `.png`, and `.webp`. Import query options can request widths, formats, and quality:

      ```ruby
      Hero = import("hero.jpg?width=320,640&format=webp,jpeg&quality=82")
      ```

      Image values expose `src`, dimensions, `variants`, `srcset`, and `sizes`. Generated variants are deduplicated by source path, source hash, width, format, and quality.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Google Fonts" }
    :markdown
      `GoogleFontsPlugin` resolves Google Fonts CSS imports, downloads the raw CSS, rewrites `fonts.gstatic.com` URLs to local emitted font assets, and emits the rewritten stylesheet as a normal CSS asset. Font files are lazy IO-generated assets so downloads can overlap with CPU-bound image generation without becoming unbounded.
